# Normalise every text file to LF in the working tree, not just in the
# repository.
#
# Without this, git's autocrlf checks out CRLF on Windows while storing LF,
# so the files ruff lints locally are not the files ruff lints in CI. That
# is not a theoretical difference: ruff 0.16.4's import-sorting rule (I001)
# reports errors on the LF content that it does not report on the identical
# CRLF content. CI failed on 15 errors that `ruff check src tests` had just
# passed locally, on the same pinned ruff version and the same commit.
#
# With eol=lf the working tree matches the repository, and therefore matches
# CI, so a local check means something.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.mp4 binary
*.pdf binary
*.npz binary
*.pkl binary
*.safetensors binary
